  {
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5a3d82ac-5b27-5010-b0ba-5f4dcc251a30",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $2$ pivots in the $1$st and $2$nd columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
