    "question": {
      ":question/id": "46bd8b17-75cc-5175-8b2f-92db89f3c796",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 & -5 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 & -5 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $3$rd and $4$th columns.",
